  "content": "Domestic flights resume from TIA\nOnlinekhabar\nSunday, October 5, 2025\n0\nComments\nKathmandu, October 5\nDomestic flights that had been suspended, due to the continuous\nrainfall\nsince yesterday have resumed early Sunday morning. The\nTribhuvan International Airport\noffice reported that domestic flights have resumed in areas where weather conditions are favorable.\nAccording to the airport office, flights from Kathmandu to Nepalgunj and Bhadrapur have already taken off this morning.\nThe office further stated that domestic flights have resumed after receiving reports that weather conditions in Pokhara and Surkhet are also suitable for air travel.\nHowever, international flights have been operating regularly since last evening.\nReact to this post\nHot Topics\nEverest\ndisaster\nnatural disaster\nheavy snowfall\nConversation\nNew\nOld\nPopular\nAdd Comment\nLogin to comment\nRemenber me\nForgot password?\nLogin\nNot have account yet?\nSignup Now\nOr use Social Media?\nGoogle\nFacebook\nTwitter\nForgot Password?\nSend Password Reset Link\nBack\nRelated News\nLong-distance travel from Kathmandu remains suspended, tickets to be refunded\n1 day ago\nHeavy rainfall expected in many parts of Nepal until Wednesday as monsoon remains active\n2 months ago\nHeavy rainfall forecast in some places today\n3 months ago\nDisaster authority warns of heavy rainfall, urges caution for travelers\n1 year ago\nNepal braces for heavy rainfall, 27 districts on high alert\n1 year ago\nHeavy rainfall forecast in parts of 4 Provinces, public advised to stay alert\n1 year ago\nMost Read\nVarious ways you can enjoy goat meat this Dashain festival\nHighways blocked nationwide as heavy rainfall disrupts travel\nNepalis celebrate Bijaya Dashami, auspicious Tika time set at 11:53 am\nManaslu climbing in autumn starts on encouraging note; Nima Chhiring sets new record\nMonsoon triggers flood and landslide risks in several districts, DHM issues special alert\nSubscribe to our newsletter\nSubscribe to Onlinekhabar English to get notified of exclusive news stories.\nEditor's Pick\nEditor's Pick\n4 government buildings, including Supreme Court, declared unfit for use\n2 weeks ago\nEditor's Pick\nCharred body found at Koteshwor Bhatbhateni, Gen-Z protest death toll rises to 74\n3 weeks ago\nEditor's Pick\nNo consensus on Hami Nepal’s claim of leading the Gen-Z movement\n3 weeks ago\nEditor's Pick\nDecades-old irrigation projects stall as Madhesh faces drought, food crisis looms\n2 months ago\nEditor's Pick\nNepal’s farming crisis: When plans stay on paper and fields suffer\n2 months ago\nAlso Read\nDisaster\nHundreds stranded on Everest’s eastern side after heavy snowfall\n1 hour ago\nDisaster\nFloods and landslides obstruct roads at 19 locations in Koshi and Bagmati Provinces\n3 hours ago\nDisaster\nDeath toll from landslides and floods rises to 52 across Nepal\n17 hours ago\nDisaster\nHeavy rain risk eases in Kathmandu Valley, shifts to Koshi Province\n1 day ago\nOpinion\nAnalysing Nepal’s performance in the Unity Cup\n1 day ago",
